---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Caseload Math — Free Capacity Call for Law Firm Owners"
  description="How to know your case manager is drowning before a client tells you. Book a free call and run the capacity math on your own case managers."
  noindex={true}
  schema={{
    "@type": "WebPage",
    "name": "Caseload Math",
    "description": "A free capacity call for law firm owners, built around the arithmetic of case manager capacity.",
    "publisher": {
      "@type": "Organization",
      "name": "Attorney Assistant"
    }
  }}
>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════
       HERO
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-brand-950 min-h-[90vh] flex items-center">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-br from-brand-navy via-brand-900 to-brand-950"></div>
    <div class="lp-orb lp-orb--1" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="lp-orb lp-orb--2" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="lp-orb lp-orb--3" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="grain-overlay"></div>

    <div class="absolute inset-0 z-[1] opacity-[0.03]" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="absolute inset-0" style="background-image: linear-gradient(rgba(255,255,255,0.5) 1px, transparent 1px), linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(255,255,255,0.5) 1px, transparent 1px); background-size: 60px 60px;"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="container-wide relative z-10 py-20 lg:py-28">
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 lg:gap-16 items-start">
        <div class="reveal">
          <div class="mb-5">
            <span class="lp-pulse-badge">
              <span class="lp-pulse-dot"></span>
              For Law Firm Owners
            </span>
          </div>
          <h1 class="text-display-md md:text-display-lg lg:text-display-xl font-heading text-white leading-tight mb-5">
            Your case manager isn't slow. <span class="text-gradient-gold">They're over capacity.</span>
          </h1>
          <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-gray-300 mb-8 leading-relaxed">
            How to know a case manager is drowning before a client tells you &mdash; the arithmetic that turns a feeling into a hiring decision.
          </p>

          <!-- Stat ticker -->
          <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-10">
            <div class="lp-hero-stat">
              <span class="lp-hero-stat-num lp-count" data-target="8">0</span>
              <span class="lp-hero-stat-label">signs a case manager is already past capacity</span>
            </div>
            <div class="lp-hero-stat">
              <span class="lp-hero-stat-num lp-count" data-target="150">0</span>
              <span class="lp-hero-stat-label">working hours a month, the real supply number</span>
            </div>
            <div class="lp-hero-stat">
              <span class="lp-hero-stat-num lp-count" data-target="116">0</span>
              <span class="lp-hero-stat-label">hours a month over capacity in one firm's worked example</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- What the call covers -->
          <div class="space-y-4 mb-10">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-widest">On Your Call We'll Cover</p>
            <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
              <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-brand-gold/10 flex items-center justify-center mt-0.5">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-brand-gold" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M3.75 13.5l10.5-11.25L12 10.5h8.25L9.75 21.75 12 13.5H3.75z" /></svg>
              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="text-base font-semibold text-white">Your actual capacity in files, not a guess</p>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-0.5">Available hours divided by average hours per file. We'll run it live with your numbers.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
              <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-brand-gold/10 flex items-center justify-center mt-0.5">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-brand-gold" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M2.25 18L9 11.25l4.306 4.306a11.95 11.95 0 015.814-5.518l2.74-1.22m0 0l-5.94-2.281m5.94 2.28l-2.28 5.941" /></svg>
              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="text-base font-semibold text-white">The gap in hours and in seats</p>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-0.5">The exact number you can take to a hiring decision, instead of a feeling that someone seems overwhelmed.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
              <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-brand-gold/10 flex items-center justify-center mt-0.5">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-brand-gold" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M6.75 3v2.25M17.25 3v2.25M3 18.75V7.5a2.25 2.25 0 012.25-2.25h13.5A2.25 2.25 0 0121 7.5v11.25m-18 0A2.25 2.25 0 005.25 21h13.5A2.25 2.25 0 0021 18.75m-18 0v-7.5A2.25 2.25 0 015.25 9h13.5A2.25 2.25 0 0121 11.25v7.5" /></svg>
              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="text-base font-semibold text-white">Three ways to close the gap</p>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-0.5">Cut hours per file, split the role, or add a seat &mdash; and which one fits your firm right now.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 text-sm text-gray-400">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-brand-gold" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M16.704 4.153a.75.75 0 01.143 1.052l-8 10.5a.75.75 0 01-1.127.075l-4.5-4.5a.75.75 0 011.06-1.06l3.894 3.893 7.48-9.817a.75.75 0 011.05-.143z" clip-rule="evenodd" /></svg>
              Free &mdash; 30 minutes
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-brand-gold" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M16.704 4.153a.75.75 0 01.143 1.052l-8 10.5a.75.75 0 01-1.127.075l-4.5-4.5a.75.75 0 011.06-1.06l3.894 3.893 7.48-9.817a.75.75 0 011.05-.143z" clip-rule="evenodd" /></svg>
              No commitment
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-brand-gold" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M16.704 4.153a.75.75 0 01.143 1.052l-8 10.5a.75.75 0 01-1.127.075l-4.5-4.5a.75.75 0 011.06-1.06l3.894 3.893 7.48-9.817a.75.75 0 011.05-.143z" clip-rule="evenodd" /></svg>
              Built inside a working law firm
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Booking Widget -->
        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-1 shadow-2xl ring-1 ring-white/10 reveal lp-widget-glow" style="transition-delay: 150ms" id="book-now">
          <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-4 md:p-5">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
              <div class="featured-icon featured-icon-md featured-icon-gold">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M6.75 3v2.25M17.25 3v2.25M3 18.75V7.5a2.25 2.25 0 012.25-2.25h13.5A2.25 2.25 0 0121 7.5v11.25m-18 0A2.25 2.25 0 005.25 21h13.5A2.25 2.25 0 0021 18.75m-18 0v-7.5A2.25 2.25 0 015.25 9h13.5A2.25 2.25 0 0121 11.25v7.5" /></svg>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h2 class="text-lg font-heading text-gray-900">Book Your Capacity Call</h2>
                <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">Free &mdash; 30 minutes</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="meetings-iframe-container" data-src="https://meet.attorneyassistant.com/meetings/attorney-assistant/magnet-caseload-math-playbook?embed=true"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="absolute bottom-8 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 z-10 lp-scroll-hint" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="w-6 h-10 rounded-full border-2 border-white/20 flex justify-center pt-2">
        <div class="w-1 h-2.5 bg-brand-gold rounded-full lp-scroll-dot"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════
       OPENING — the story + eight signs
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-gray-950 lp-section-lg">
    <div class="absolute inset-0">
      <div class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-[500px] h-[500px] bg-brand-gold/5 rounded-full blur-[120px]"></div>
      <div class="absolute bottom-0 left-0 w-[400px] h-[400px] bg-red-500/3 rounded-full blur-[100px]"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="grain-overlay"></div>

    <div class="container-wide relative z-10">
      <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 lg:gap-20 items-center">
        <!-- Left: Story -->
        <div class="reveal">
          <span class="badge bg-brand-gold/15 text-brand-gold border-brand-gold/20 mb-6">Read This First</span>
          <h2 class="text-display-sm md:text-display-md font-heading text-white mb-5 leading-tight">
            Here's how most firms find out a case manager is drowning.
          </h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-400 leading-relaxed mb-6">
            A client calls the owner directly because nobody returned three messages. Records are 60 days late on a file nobody looked at. A deadline reminder fires on a matter that was never calendared. The owner steps in, fixes the file, and quietly wonders whether the case manager is any good.
          </p>
          <p class="text-base text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-6">
            The case manager is fine. They have 140 open files and the capacity for 90. Nothing on the list of symptoms is a performance problem. All of it is arithmetic.
          </p>
          <p class="text-xl font-heading text-brand-gold">
            Nobody quits because the work is hard. They quit because there's more of it than any person could do.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Right: four of the eight signs -->
        <div class="reveal space-y-4" style="transition-delay: 150ms">
          <div class="lp-pain-card lp-pain-card--stagger-1">
            <div class="lp-pain-icon">
              <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M2.25 6.75c0 8.284 6.716 15 15 15h2.25a2.25 2.25 0 002.25-2.25v-1.372c0-.516-.351-.966-.852-1.091l-4.423-1.106c-.44-.11-.902.055-1.173.417l-.97 1.293c-.282.376-.769.542-1.21.38a12.035 12.035 0 01-7.143-7.143c-.162-.441.004-.928.38-1.21l1.293-.97c.363-.271.527-.734.417-1.173L6.963 3.102a1.125 1.125 0 00-1.091-.852H4.5A2.25 2.25 0 002.25 4.5v2.25z" /></svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="text-white font-heading text-base">Clients call the attorney for updates</p>
              <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">The scheduled update didn't happen.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="lp-pain-card lp-pain-card--stagger-2">
            <div class="lp-pain-icon">
              <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 6v6h4.5m4.5 0a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" /></svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="text-white font-heading text-base">Records requests sit past 30 days</p>
              <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Follow-up is the first task that gets dropped.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="lp-pain-card lp-pain-card--stagger-3">
            <div class="lp-pain-icon">
              <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M2.25 18.75a60.07 60.07 0 0115.797 2.101c.727.198 1.453-.342 1.453-1.096V18.75M3.75 4.5v.75A.75.75 0 013 6h-.75m0 0v-.375c0-.621.504-1.125 1.125-1.125H20.25M2.25 6v9m18-10.5v.75c0 .414.336.75.75.75h.75m-1.5-1.5h.375c.621 0 1.125.504 1.125 1.125v9.75c0 .621-.504 1.125-1.125 1.125h-.375m1.5-1.5H21a.75.75 0 00-.75.75v.75m0 0H3.75m0 0h-.375a1.125 1.125 0 01-1.125-1.125V15m1.5 1.5v-.75A.75.75 0 003 15h-.75M15 10.5a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0zm3 0h.008v.008H18V10.5zm-12 0h.008v.008H6V10.5z" /></svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="text-white font-heading text-base">Files have no activity note for 30+ days</p>
              <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Not stalled files. Forgotten ones.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="lp-pain-card" style="animation: lpSlideIn 0.5s ease 0.55s both;">
            <div class="lp-pain-icon">
              <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 6.75h.007v.008H12V6.75zm.375 6a9.75 9.75 0 100-13.5 9.75 9.75 0 000 13.5z" /></svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="text-white font-heading text-base">The case manager works weekends to catch up</p>
              <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Catching up never ends.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="lp-quote-banner mt-14 max-w-3xl mx-auto reveal">
        &ldquo;Five or more signs checked: you are already losing files and probably about to lose a person.&rdquo;
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════
       THE MATH
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-white lp-section-lg">
    <div class="absolute top-0 left-0 w-full h-1 bg-gradient-to-r from-red-500 via-brand-gold to-brand-blue"></div>
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="text-center mb-12 reveal">
        <span class="badge bg-brand-navy/10 text-brand-navy border-brand-navy/15 mb-4">Do This Before You Read Further</span>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm md:text-display-md font-heading text-gray-900 mb-4">
          Capacity is hours, not file count.
        </h2>
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-500 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
          A case manager has about 1,800 working hours a year after holidays, PTO, meetings, and interruptions. Roughly 150 hours a month. That's the supply. The demand is the number of hours your files actually need.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-5 reveal mb-10 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <div class="flex gap-4 p-5 rounded-xl bg-gray-50 border border-gray-100">
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-brand-navy/10 flex items-center justify-center text-brand-navy font-heading font-bold">A</div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-heading text-gray-900 mb-1">Available hours per month per case manager</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">Paid hours minus PTO, holidays, meetings, and training. Most firms land between 140 and 150.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4 p-5 rounded-xl bg-gray-50 border border-gray-100">
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-brand-navy/10 flex items-center justify-center text-brand-navy font-heading font-bold">B</div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-heading text-gray-900 mb-1">Hours per file per month, by stage</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">Pre-litigation might take 3 to 4 hours a month. Litigation, 6 to 10. Awaiting disbursement, under 1. Use your own numbers.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="lp-rule-box max-w-3xl mx-auto reveal mb-10 text-center">
        <span class="lp-rule-box-label">The Formula</span>
        <p class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-heading text-brand-navy font-mono">Capacity (files) = Available hours per month &divide; Average hours per file per month</p>
      </div>

      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto reveal mb-10 rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 overflow-hidden">
        <div class="bg-brand-navy text-white text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest px-5 py-3 flex justify-between">
          <span>Worked Example</span>
          <span class="text-white/60 normal-case font-normal">2 case managers, 115 open files</span>
        </div>
        <div class="divide-y divide-gray-100">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-3 text-sm">
            <span class="text-gray-600">Available hours per month</span>
            <span class="font-semibold text-gray-900">294</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-3 text-sm">
            <span class="text-gray-600">Total hours needed per month</span>
            <span class="font-semibold text-gray-900">410</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-3 text-sm">
            <span class="text-gray-600">Capacity in files at this mix</span>
            <span class="font-semibold text-gray-900">82 files (actual: 115)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-3 text-sm">
            <span class="text-gray-600">Seats needed at this mix</span>
            <span class="font-semibold text-gray-900">2.8, round up to 3</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-4 bg-brand-gold/10">
            <span class="font-heading text-gray-900">Gap</span>
            <span class="font-heading text-2xl text-brand-navy">116 hrs/mo over capacity</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="lp-quote-banner max-w-2xl mx-auto reveal mb-10">
        &ldquo;This firm is running two people at the workload of nearly three. The gap is roughly 29 hours a week of work not getting done.&rdquo;
      </div>
      <p class="text-center text-lg font-heading text-gray-900 max-w-2xl mx-auto reveal">
        Run your own number before the call. Everything else is an opinion until you have it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════
       THREE WAYS TO CLOSE THE GAP
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden lp-section-lg">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-br from-brand-navy via-brand-900 to-brand-950"></div>
    <div class="absolute top-20 right-0 w-[500px] h-[500px] bg-brand-gold/8 rounded-full blur-[100px]"></div>
    <div class="absolute bottom-0 left-0 w-[400px] h-[400px] bg-brand-blue/8 rounded-full blur-[100px]"></div>
    <div class="grain-overlay"></div>

    <div class="container-wide relative z-10">
      <div class="text-center mb-10 reveal">
        <span class="badge bg-brand-gold/15 text-brand-gold border-brand-gold/20 mb-4">Closing The Gap</span>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm md:text-display-md font-heading text-white mb-5">
          Three ways to close it. <span class="text-gradient-gold">Pick deliberately.</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-400 max-w-2xl mx-auto">Most firms past capacity need the first and the third together. The first alone delays the hire by a quarter. It doesn't replace it.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto reveal mb-14">
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center gap-2 sm:gap-4 py-5 border-b border-white/10">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 sm:w-48 flex-shrink-0">
            <span class="w-9 h-9 rounded-full bg-brand-blue/20 flex items-center justify-center text-brand-blue font-heading font-bold flex-shrink-0">1</span>
            <p class="text-[11px] font-bold text-brand-blue uppercase tracking-widest">Option 1</p>
          </div>
          <div class="flex-1">
            <h3 class="text-white font-heading text-base mb-1">Cut hours per file</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm">Standardize the status update. Template the records request. Firms that document their process cut 15 to 25 percent of hours per file. It is never enough on its own past a certain volume.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center gap-2 sm:gap-4 py-5 border-b border-white/10">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 sm:w-48 flex-shrink-0">
            <span class="w-9 h-9 rounded-full bg-brand-gold/20 flex items-center justify-center text-brand-gold font-heading font-bold flex-shrink-0">2</span>
            <p class="text-[11px] font-bold text-brand-gold uppercase tracking-widest">Option 2</p>
          </div>
          <div class="flex-1">
            <h3 class="text-white font-heading text-base mb-1">Split the role</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm">One person owning client communication, records, and documents across 100 files is three jobs. Pull records and scheduling into an admin seat, cheaper to fill and faster to onboard.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center gap-2 sm:gap-4 py-5">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 sm:w-48 flex-shrink-0">
            <span class="w-9 h-9 rounded-full bg-white/10 flex items-center justify-center text-white font-heading font-bold flex-shrink-0">3</span>
            <p class="text-[11px] font-bold text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-widest">Option 3</p>
          </div>
          <div class="flex-1">
            <h3 class="text-white font-heading text-base mb-1">Add a seat</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm">When the calculator says 2.8 seats and you have 2, you need a third person. A trained remote case manager removes the recruiting cycle and lands at a fraction of the cost of adding the seat after a client leaves.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-5 reveal mb-6">
        <div class="lp-stat-box lp-stat-box--highlight">
          <div class="lp-stat-box-num lp-stat-box-num--gold">97%</div>
          <p class="lp-stat-box-label">Answer rate 24/7, up from 82%</p>
        </div>
        <div class="lp-stat-box lp-stat-box--highlight">
          <div class="lp-stat-box-num lp-stat-box-num--gold">15 min</div>
          <p class="lp-stat-box-label">Max speed to lead, down from 34</p>
        </div>
        <div class="lp-stat-box lp-stat-box--highlight">
          <div class="lp-stat-box-num lp-stat-box-num--gold">6</div>
          <p class="lp-stat-box-label">Follow-up touches in 3 days</p>
        </div>
        <div class="lp-stat-box lp-stat-box--highlight">
          <div class="lp-stat-box-num lp-stat-box-num--gold">109</div>
          <p class="lp-stat-box-label">Cases signed by one staff member in 30 days</p>
        </div>
      </div>
